    "name_ja": "ギンザメ",
    "scientific_name": "Chimaera phantasma",
    "habitat": "continental_slope",
    "order": 26,
    "notes": "Silver chimaera (ghost shark): big blunt triangular head with large eyes and a small underslung mouth with crushing tooth plates, large wing-like pectoral fins it flaps to swim, a tall narrow first dorsal fin with a venomous spine at its front, a long low second dorsal, and a body tapering to a long whip-like tail; silvery with dark lateral bands. Approximations: the spine is the leading edge of the first dorsal (apex at the front); tooth plates are two short incisor-like teeth; the lateral bands are left to countershading."
